From: Asius <peeter@asius.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: do not drop the LE setup reference on encryption

A bonded iPhone can finish encryption before remote features arrive. The
BT_CONFIG path in hci_encrypt_cfm confirms the connection and drops a setup
reference. For LE, that reference belongs to hci_le_read_remote_features.
Its completion drops the same reference again, scheduling a disconnect
four seconds later despite an active ATT socket.

Keep the existing connection confirmation. Only drop the classic ACL setup
reference here. The LE features request retains ownership of its reference.

diff --git a/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h b/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
--- a/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
+++ b/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
@@ -2190,7 +2190,11 @@ static inline void hci_encrypt_cfm(struct hci_conn *conn, __u8 status)
 			conn->state = BT_CONNECTED;
 
 		hci_connect_cfm(conn, status);
-		hci_conn_drop(conn);
+		/* LE setup is held by the remote-features request. Its
+		 * completion releases that reference, even after encryption.
+		 */
+		if (conn->type == ACL_LINK)
+			hci_conn_drop(conn);
 		return;
 	}
 
